#Main,Sub,Name,Cause,Treatment
0,0,Normal,Normal,Normal
11,0,Control power supply under-voltage,Voltage between P and N of the converter portion of the control power supply has fallen below the specified value.,Measure the voltage between lines of connector and terminal block (L1C - L2C).
,,,(1) Power supply voltage is low. Instantaneous power failure has occurred.,(1) Increase the power capacity. Change the power supply.
,,,(2) Lack of power capacity...Power supply voltage has fallen down due to inrush current at the main power-on.,(2) Increase the power capacity.
,,,(3) Failure of servo driver (failure of the circuit),(3) Replace the driver with a new one.
12,0,Over-voltage,Voltage between P and N of the converter portion of the control power supply has exceeded the specified value.,"Measure the voltage between lines of connector (L1, L2 and L3)."
,,,(1)Power supply voltage has exceeded the permissible input voltage. Voltage surge due to the phase-advancing capacitor or UPS (Uninterruptible Power Supply) have occurred.,(1) Enter correct voltage. Remove a phaseadvancing capacitor.
,,,(2) Disconnection of the regeneration discharge resistor,(2) Measure the resistance of the external resistor connected between terminal P and B of the driver. Replace the external resistor if the value is ¡Ä.
,,,(3) External regeneration discharge resistor is not appropriate and could not absorb the regeneration energy,(3) Change to the one with specified resistance and wattage.
,,,(4) Failure of servo driver (failure of the circuit),(4) Replace the driver with a new one.
13,0,Main power supply under-voltage (PN),The voltage between P and N of the converter portion of the main power supply has fallen below the specified value during Servo-ON.,"Measure the voltage between lines of connector (L1, L2 and L3)."
,,,(1) Power supply voltage is low. Instantaneous power failure has occurred.,"(1) Increase the power capacity. Change the power supply. Remove the causes of the shutdown of the magnetic contactor or the main power supply, then re-enter the power."
,,,(2) Lack of power capacity...Power supply voltage has fallen down due to inrush current at the main power-on.,(2) Increase the power capacity.
,,,(3) Phase lack...3-phase input driver has been operated with single phase input.,"(3) Connect each phase of the power supply (L1, L2 and L3) correctly."
,,,(4) Failure of servo driver (failure of the circuit),(4) Replace the driver with a new one.
13,1,Main power supply under-voltage (AC-off),Instantaneous power failure has occurred between L1 and L3 for longer period than the preset time with Pr5.09 (Detection time of main power off) while Pr5.08 (LV trip selection at main power off) is set to 1.,"Measure the voltage between lines of connector (L1, L2 and L3)."
,,,(1) Power supply voltage is low. Instantaneous power failure has occurred.,"(1) Increase the power capacity. Change the power supply. Remove the causes of the shutdown of the magnetic contactor or the main power supply, then re-enter the power."
,,,(2) Instantaneous power failure has occurred.,(2) Set up the longer time to Pr5.09 (Detection time of main power off). Set up each phase of the power correctly.
,,,(3) Lack of power capacity...Power supply voltage has fallen down due to inrush current at the main power-on.,(3) Increase the power capacity.
,,,(4) Phase lack...3-phase input driver has been operated with single phase input.,"(4) For single phase, 100V and 200V driver, use L1 and L3."
,,,(5) Failure of servo driver (failure of the circuit),(5) Replace the driver with a new one.
14,0,Over-current,Current through the converter portion has exceeded the specified value.,Check a short circuit and earth fault of the wiring.
,,,"(1)  Failure of servo driver (failure of the circuit, IGBT or other components).","(1) Turn to Servo-ON, while disconnecting the motor. If error occurs immediately, replace with a new driver."
,,,"(2) Short of the motor wire (U, V and W).","(2) Check that the motor wire (U, V and W) is not shorted, and check the branched out wire out of the connector. Make a correct wiring connection."
,,,(3) Earth fault of the motor wire.,"(3) Measure the insulation resistance between motor wires, U, V and W and earth wire. In case of poor insulation, replace the motor."
,,,(4) Burnout of the motor.,"(4) Check the balance of resister between each motor line, and if unbalance is found, replace the motor."
,,,(5) Poor contact of the motor wire.,"(5) Check the loose connectors. If they are, or pulled out, fix them securely."
,,,(6) Melting of the relays for dynamic brake due to frequent Servo-ON/OFF operation.,(6) Replace the driver. Prohibit the run/stop operation with Servo-ON/OFF.
,,,(7) The motor is not applicable to the driver.,"(7) Check the name plate and capacity of the motor and driver, and replace with motor applicable to the driver."
,,,(8) Timing of pulse input is same as or earlier than Servo-ON.,(8) Enter the pulses 100ms or longer after Servo-ON.
,,,(9) Overheating of the dynamic brake circuit (F-frame only).,(9) Discontinue the run/stop operation with Servo ON-OFF. Allow approx. 3 minutes pause when the dynamic brake is activated during highspeed running.
14,1,IPM error,Current through the converter portion has exceeded the specified value.,Check the short circuit and earth fault of the wiring.
,,,"(1)  Failure of servo driver (failure of the circuit, IGBT or other components).","(1) Turn to Servo-ON, while disconnecting the motor. If error occurs immediately, replace with a new driver."
,,,"(2) Short of the motor wire (U, V and W).","(2) Check that the motor wire (U, V and W) is not shorted, and check the branched out wire out of the connector. Make a correct wiring connection."
,,,(3) Earth fault of the motor wire.,"(3) Measure the insulation resistance between motor wires, U, V and W and earth wire. In case of poor insulation, replace the motor."
,,,(4) Burnout of the motor.,"(4) Check the balance of resister between each motor line, and if unbalance is found, replace the motor."
,,,(5) Poor contact of the motor wire.,"(5) Check the loose connectors. If they are, or pulled out, fix them securely."
,,,(6) Melting of the relays for dynamic brake due to frequent Servo-ON/OFF operation.,(6) Replace the driver. Prohibit the run/stop operation with Servo-ON/OFF.
,,,(7) The motor is not applicable to the driver.,"(7) Check the name plate and capacity of the motor and driver, and replace with motor applicable to the driver."
,,,(8) Timing of pulse input is same as or earlier than Servo-ON.,(8) Enter the pulses 100ms or longer after Servo-ON.
,,,(9) Overheating of the dynamic brake circuit (F-frame only).,(9) Discontinue the run/stop operation with Servo ON-OFF. Allow approx. 3 minutes pause when the dynamic brake is activated during highspeed running.
15,0,Over-heat,Temperature of the heat sink or power device has been risen over the specified temperature.,Check the use temperature range of the driver.
,,,(1) Ambient temperature has risen over the specified temperature.,(1) Improve the ambient temperature and cooling condition.
,,,(2) Over-load.,(2) Increase the capacity of the driver and motor. Set up longer acceleration/deceleration time. Lower the load.
16,0,Over-load,Torque  command value has exceeded the over-load level set with Pr5.12 (Over-load level setup) and resulted in overload protection according to the time characteristics (described later).,Check that the torque  (current) does not oscillates nor fluctuate up an down very much on the graphic screen of the PANATERM. Check the over-load alarm display and load factor with the PANATERM.
,,,(1) Load was heavy and actual torque has exceeded the rated torque  and kept running for a long time.,(1) Increase the capacity of the driver and motor. Set up longer acceleration/deceleration time. Lower the load.
,,,"(2) Oscillation and hunching action due to poor adjustment. Motor vibration, abnormal noise. Pr0.04 (Inertia ratio) setup error.",(2) Make a re-adjustment.
,,,"(3) Miswiring, disconnection of the motor.",(3) Make a wiring as per the wiring diagram. Replace the cables.
,,,(4) Machine has collided or the load has gotten heavy. Machine has been distorted.,(4) Remove the cause of distortion. Lower the load.
,,,(5) Electromagnetic brake has been kept engaged.,(5) Measure the voltage between brake terminals. Release the brake.
,,,"(6) While wiring multiple axes, miswiring has occurred by connecting the motor cable to other axis.",(6) Make a correct wiring by matching the correct motor and feedback scale wires.
,,,(7) Pr5.12 (Over-load level setup) is too low.,(7) Set up Pr5.12 (Over-load level setup) to 0.
16,1,Torque saturation error protection,Torque saturated has continued for the period set to Pr9.35 (Torque saturation error protection frequency).,Check the operating state of the amplifier.
,,,,Check to see if the motor wire is disconnected.
18,0,Regenerative resistor over-load,Regenerative energy has exceeded the capacity of regenerative resistor,Check the load factor of the regenerative resistor from the front panel or via communication. Do not use in the continuous regenerative brake application.
,,,"(1) Due to the regenerative energy during deceleration caused by a large load inertia, and converter voltage has risen.",(1) Check the running pattern (velocity monitor). Check the load factor of the regenerative resistor and over-regeneration warning display. 
,,,And the voltage is risen further due to the lack of capacity of absorbing this energy of the regeneration discharge resistor.,"Increase the capacity of the driver and the motor, and loosen the deceleration time. Use the external regenerative resistor."
,,,(2) Regenerative energy has not been absorbed in the specified time due to a high motor operational speed.,"(2) Check the running pattern (speed monitor). Check the load factor of the regenerative resistor. Increase the capacity of the driver and the motor, and loosen the deceleration time. "
,,,,Lower the motor rotational speed. Use an external regenerative resistor.
,,,(3) Active limit of the external regenerative resistor has been limited to 10% duty.,(3) Set up Pr0.16 (External regenerative resistor setup).
18,1,Regenerative transistor error,Regenerative driver transistor on the servo driver is defective.,Replace the driver.
24,0,Position deviation excess,Deviation pulses have exceeded the setup of Pr0.14 (Position deviation excess setup).,Check the movement of the motor.
,,,(1) The motor movement has not followed the command.,(1) Check that the motor follows to the position command pulses.
,,,,Check that the output torque has not saturated in torque monitor. Make a gain adjustment.
,,,,Set up maximum value to Pr0.13 (1st torque limit) and Pr5.22 (2nd torque limit).
,,,,Make a feedback scale wiring as per the wiring diagram. Set up the longer acceleration/deceleration time. Lower the load and speed.
,,,(2) Setup value of Pr0.14 (Position deviation excess setup) is small.,(2) Set up a larger value to Pr0.14 (Position deviation excess setup). Or Set up to 0 and invalidate it.
24,1,Velocity deviation excess,Commanded speed error has exceeded the setup value of Pr6.02 (Velocity deviation excess setup).,"Check the movement of the motor.
Set up a larger value to Pr6.02 (Velocity deviation excess setup). Or Set up to 0 and invalidate it."
26,0,Over-speed,The motor speed has exceeded the setup value of Pr5.13 (Over-speed level setup).,Make a gain adjustment when an overshoot has occurred due to a poor gain adjustment.
,,,,Do not give an excessive speed command.
,,,,Check the command pulse input frequency and division/multiplication ratio.
,,,,Make a wiring connection of the feedback scale as per the wiring diagram.
,,,,Set up Pr5.13 (Over-speed level setup) to 0. (Set up the best number of revolutions of the motor to 1.2 times)
26,1,2nd Over-speed,The motor speed has exceeded the setup value of Pr6.15 (2nd over-speed level setup).,Make a gain adjustment when an overshoot has occurred due to a poor gain adjustment.
,,,,Do not give an excessive speed command.
,,,,Check the command pulse input frequency and division/multiplication ratio.
,,,,Make a wiring connection of the feedback scale as per the wiring diagram.
,,,,Set up Pr6.15 (2nd over-speed level setup).
27,4,Command error,Position command variation (value after electronic gear) exceeds the specified value.,Check whether the position command was significantly changed due to cyclic position control (CP).
,,,,Check electronic gear ratio.
27,5,Command generation error,Position command generation process exceeded the computation range.,Make sure that the electronic gear ratio and velocity control conform to limit requirements.
27,6,Motion commands conflict,FFT operated only by the driver: RTEX communication was established during trial run.,FFT: check if RTEX communication was established during trial run.
27,7,Position data initialization error,"During validation mode of attribute C parameter of reset command of RTEX communication, servo was turned ON.",Check to see that the servo is OFF during validation mode of attribute C parameter of reset command of RTEX communication.
28,0,Over-frequency pulse output,The output frequency of pulse regeneration has exceeded the limit.,"Check the setup values of Pr0.11(Numerator of pulse
output division) and Pr5.03 (Denominator of pulse output division)."
,,,,"To disable the detection, set Pr5.33 (Pulse regenerative output limit setup) to 0."
29,1,Counter overflow 1,"After turning on of control power in absolute mode, after CONFIG, after FFT or after trial run: during position information initialization process, absolute encoder (absolute scale) position (pulse unit)/electronic gear ratio exceeded ¡¾2^31 (2147483648).",Check the operation range at the position of absolute encoder (absolute scale) and electronic gear ratio.
29,2,Counter overflow 2,Position deviation in unit of pulse has exceeded ¡¾2^29 (536870912).,Check that the motor follows the position command pulses.
,,,"Or, position deviation in unit of command has exceeded ¡¾2^30 (1073741824).",Check that the output torque has not saturated in torque monitor.
,,,,Make a gain adjustment.
,,,,Set up maximum value to torque limit setting.
,,,,Make a wiring connection of the feedback scale as per the wiring diagram.
29,3,Counter overflow 3,Return to home final running distance x electronic gear ratio has exceeded ¡¾2^31 (2147483648).,Review the return to home final running distance and the electronic gear ratio.
30,0,Safety input,Input photocoupler of both or one of safety input 1 and 2 is OFF.,Check wiring of safety input 1 and 2.
33,0,Input duplicated allocation error 1,"Input signals (SI1, SI2, SI3, SI4) are assigned with two functions.",Allocate correct function to each connector pin.
33,1,Input duplicated allocation error 2,"Input signals (SI5, SI6, SI7, SI8) are assigned with two functions.",Allocate correct function to each connector pin.
33,2,Input function number error 1,"Input signals (SI1, SI2, SI3, SI4) are assigned with undefined number. Or, logical setup is not correct.",Allocate correct function to each connector pin.
33,3,Input function number error 2,"Input signals (SI5, SI6, SI7, SI8) are assigned with undefined number. Or, logical setup is not correct.",Allocate correct function to each connector pin.
33,4,Output function number error 1,Output signals (SO1) are assigned with undefined number.,Allocate correct function to each connector pin.
33,5,Output function number error 2,Output signals (SO2) are assigned with undefined number.,Allocate correct function to each connector pin.
33,8,Latch input allocation error,"Error has occurred during function assignment of latch correction pins (SI5, SI6, and SI7).",Allocate correct function to each connector pin.
,,,(1) EXT1 must be allocated to SI5. EXT2 to SI6 and EXT3 to SI7: but these are assigned to other pins.,
,,,(2) HOME is allocated to SI6 or SI7; POT is allocated to SI5 or SI7; NOT is allocated to SI5 ot SI6.,
,,,(3) Function is allocated to b-contact.,
,,,(4) Function not allocated to one or more control modes.,
34,0,Software limit,"When a position command within the specified input range is given, the motor operates outside its working range specified in Pr5.14 (Motor working range setup).",Check the movement of the motor.
,,,(1) Gain is not appropriate.,(1) Check the gain (balance between position loop gain and speed loop gain) and Inertia ratio.
,,,(2) Pr5.14 (Motor working range setup) setup value is low.,"(2) Increase the setup value of Pr5.14 (Motor working range setup). Or, Set Pr5.14 (Motor working range setup) to 0 to disable the protective function."
36,0,EEPROM parameter error,Data in parameter storage area has been damaged when reading the data from EEPROM at power-on.,Set up all parameters again.
,,,,"If the error persists, replace the driver (it may be a failure). Return the product to the dealer or manufacturer."
36,1,EEPROM parameter error,The error was found when reading the data from EEPROM at power-on.,Set up all parameters again.
,,,,"If the error persists, replace the driver (it may be a failure). Return the product to the dealer or manufacturer."
36,2,EEPROM parameter error,Data in parameter storage area has been damaged when reading the data from EEPROM at power-on.,Set up all parameters again.
,,,,"If the error persists, replace the driver (it may be a failure). Return the product to the dealer or manufacturer."
37,0,EEPROM check code error,Data for writing confirmation to EEPROM has been damaged when reading the data from EEPROM at power-on.,Replace the driver. (it may be a failure). Return the product to a dealer or 1 manufacturer.
37,1,EEPROM check code error,Data for writing confirmation to EEPROM has been damaged when reading the data from EEPROM at power-on.,Replace the driver. (it may be a failure). Return the product to a dealer or 1 manufacturer.
37,2,EEPROM check code error,Data for writing confirmation to EEPROM has been damaged when reading the data from EEPROM at power-on.,Replace the driver. (it may be a failure). Return the product to a dealer or 1 manufacturer.
38,0,Over-travel inhibit input protection 1,"With Pr5.04 (Over-travel inhibit input setup) = 0, both CW and CCW over-travel inhibit inputs (POT/NOT) have been ON.","Check that there are not any errors in switches, wires or power supply which are connected to positive direction/ negative direction over-travel inhibit input. "
,,,"With Pr5.04 (Over-travel inhibit input setup) = 2, CW or CCW over-travel inhibit input has turned ON.",Check that the rising time of the control power supply (DC12 to 24V) is not slow.
,,,"With Pr5.04 = 0, and either of the positive and
negative over-travel inhibit input has turned ON during
the execution of magnet pole position estimation.",
,,,"With Pr5.04 = 0, and either of the positive and
negative over-travel inhibit input has turned ON during
automatic linear motor setup,",
38,1,Over-travel inhibit input protection 2,"RTEX communication is OFF with Pr5.04 (Over-travel inhibit input setup) = 0, and POT or NOT is ON, and then operation command (ex. trial run, FFT) is given through USB communication.","Check that there are not any errors in switches, wires or power supply which are connected to positive direction/ negative direction over-travel inhibit input. "
,,,"Or, POT or NOT is turned ON while the system is operating according to the command given through USB communication.",Check that the rising time of the control power supply (12 to 24 VDC) is not slow.
38,2,Over-travel inhibit input protection 3,"With POT allocated to SI6 or NOT to SI7, Pr5.04 (Over-travel inhibit input setup) is set to a value other than 1 (disabled).","When POT is allocated to SI6 or NOT allocated to SI7, make sure that Pr5.04 (Over-travel inhibit input setup) is set to 1 (disabled)."
50,0,Feedback scale wiring error,"Communication between the feedback scale and the driver has been interrupted in certain times, and disconnection detecting function has been triggered.","Make a wiring connection of the feedback scale as per the wiring diagram.
Correct the miswiring of the connector pins."
,,,,"Check to see if the feedback scale type (AB-phase, serial
incremental, serial absolute) coincides with Pr3.23
(Feedback scale type selection)."
50,1,Feedback scale communication data error,Communication error has occurred in data from the feedback scale. Mainly data error due to noise. ,Secure the power supply for the feedback scale of DC5¡¾5% (4.75 to 5.25V)...pay attention especially when the feedback scale cables are long.
,,,"Feedback scale cables are connected, but communication date has some error.",Separate the feedback scale cable and the motor cable if they are bound together.
,,,,"Connect the shield to FG...refer to wiring diagramfor
feedback scale in Reference specification SX-DSV02308."
50,2,(Feedback scale communication data error),Communication data of Feedback scal and driver are not right.,Correct the miswiring of the connector pins.
51,0,Feedback scale status 0 error,Bit 0 of the feedback scale error code (ALMC) has been turned to 1. Check the specifications of the feedback scale.,"Remove the causes of the error, then clear the feedback scale error from the front panel. And then, shut off the power to reset."
51,1,Feedback scale status 1 error,Bit 1 of the feedback scale error code (ALMC) has been turned to 1. Check the specifications of the feedback scale.,"Remove the causes of the error, then clear the feedback scale error from the front panel. And then, shut off the power to reset."
51,2,Feedback scale status 2 error,Bit 2 of the feedback scale error code (ALMC) has been turned to 1. Check the specifications of the feedback scale.,"Remove the causes of the error, then clear the feedback scale error from the front panel. And then, shut off the power to reset."
51,3,Feedback scale status 3 error,Bit 3 of the feedback scale error code (ALMC) has been turned to 1. Check the specifications of the feedback scale.,"Remove the causes of the error, then clear the feedback scale error from the front panel. And then, shut off the power to reset."
51,4,Feedback scale status 4 error,Bit 4 of the feedback scale error code (ALMC) has been turned to 1. Check the specifications of the feedback scale.,"Remove the causes of the error, then clear the feedback scale error from the front panel. And then, shut off the power to reset."
51,5,Feedback scale status 5 error,Bit 5 of the feedback scale error code (ALMC) has been turned to 1. Check the specifications of the feedback scale.,"Remove the causes of the error, then clear the feedback scale error from the front panel. And then, shut off the power to reset."
51,6,(Feedback scale status 6 error),Bit 6 of the feedback scale error code (ALMC) has been turned to 1. Check the specifications of the feedback scale.,"Remove the causes of the error, then clear the feedback scale error from the front panel. And then, shut off the power to reset."
51,7,(Feedback scale status 7 error),Bit 7 of the feedback scale error code (ALMC) has been turned to 1. Check the specifications of the feedback scale.,"Remove the causes of the error, then clear the feedback scale error from the front panel. And then, shut off the power to reset."
51,8,(Feedback scale other error),Control circuit has malfunctioned due to excess noise or other causes.,"Turn off the power once, then re-enter. If error repeats, this might be a failure."
,,,Some error has occurred inside of the driver while triggering self-diagnosis function of the driver.,"Stop using the products, and replace the motor and the driver. Return the products to the dealer or manufacturer."
55,0,A-phase connection error,"A-phase wiring in the feedback scale is defective, e.g. discontinued.",Check the A-phase wiring connection of feedback scale.
55,1,B-phase connection error,"B-phase wiring in the feedback scale is defective, e.g. discontinued.",Check the B-phase wiring connection of feedback scale.
55,2,Z-phase connection error,"Z-phase wiring in the feedback scale is defective, e.g. discontinued.",Check the Z-phase wiring connection of feedback scale.
55,3,CS signal logic error,"There is an error in CS signal logic.
(All of CS signals 1, 2, and 3 are high or low)",Check the CS signal wiring connection.
55,4,AB-phase missing error,There are extremely few AB-phase pulses between CS signal changes.,"Check the CS signal, A-phase, and B-phase wiring connections."
60,0,Motor setting error,Pr9.00 (Motor type selection) = 0 has been set.,Check the setup value for Pr9.00 (Motor type selection).
,,,A setup value out of the range has been set as a setup value for Pr9.01 (Feedback scale resolution/number of scale pulse per rotation).,Check the setup value for Pr9.01 (Feedback scale resolution/number of scale pulse per rotation).
,,,"When setting Pr9.00 = 1(Linear type), Pr9.02 (Magnet pole pitch) and Pr9.30 (Number of pulses per magnet pole) has been set at the same time.","Check the setup value for each of Pr9.00 (Motor type selection), Pr9.02 (Magnet pole pitch), and Pr9.30 (Number of pulses per magnet pole)."
,,,"When setting Pr9.00 = 1 (Linear type), a value out of the range has been set as a setup value for Pr9.30 (Number of pulses per magnet pole).",Check the setup value for each of Pr9.00 (Motor type selection) and Pr9.30 (Number of pulses per magnet pole).
,,,"When setting Pr9.00 = 2 (Rotary type), Pr9.03 (Pole logarithm per rotation) = 0 has been set.",Check the setup value for each of Pr9.00 (Motor type selection) and Pr9.03 (Pole logarithm per rotation).
,,,"When setting Pr9.08 (Motor phase inductance) = 0, Pr9.12 (Automatic current response adjustment) is not 0 has been set.",Check the setup value for each of Pr9.08 (Motor phase inductance) and Pr9.12 (Automatic current response adjustment).
,,,"When setting Pr9.09 (Motor phase resistance), Pr9.12 is not 0 has been set.",Check the setup value for each of Pr9.09 (Motor phase resistance) and Pr9.12 (Automatic current response adjustment).
,,,"Number 0 has been set to each of Pr9.04 to Pr9.07, Pr9.10, and Pr9.20.","Check the setup value for each of Pr9.04 to Pr9.07, Pr9.10, and Pr9.20."
60,1,Motor combination error 1,The setup value for Pr9.06 (Rated effective motor current) is above the allowable rated current for the amplifier.,Check the setup value for Pr9.06 (Rated effective motor current) (Setting unit: 0.1 Arms).
,,,The setup value for Pr9.07 (Maximum instantaneous motor current) is above the allowable maximum current for the amplifier.,Check the setup value for Pr9.07 (Maximum instantaneous motor current) (Setting unit: 0.1 A).
,,,A value of more than 126 Mpulses has been set to the number of pulses per unit second.,"If the above setup value is not problematic, the framework for the amplifier needs to be enlarged."
,,,,Check the setup value for each of Pr9.01 (Feedback scale resolution/number of scale pulse per rotation) and Pr9.10 (Maximum over-speed level) and set a value of less than 126 M pulses to the number of pulses per unit second.
60,2,Motor combination error 2,The rated motor current is too small as against the rated amplifier current.,"Check the setup value for Pr9.06 (Rated effective motor current) (Setting unit: 0.1 Arms). If the above setup value is not problematic, the framework of the amplifier needs to be reduced."
,,,A ratio of a movable-part Inertia (M) to the rated torque (F) is too large. (The M-F ratio is too large),Check the setup value for each of Pr9.05 (Rated motor torque) (Setting unit: 0.1 N) and Pr9.04 (Moving portion Inertia of motor) (Setting unit: 0.01 kg).
,,,The automatically adjusted current-proportional integral gain is too large.,"Check the setup value for each of Pr9.06 (Rated effective motor current) (Setting unit: 0.1 Arms), Pr9.08 (Motor phase inductance) (Setting unit: 0.01 mH), and Pr9.09 (Motor phase resistance) (Setting unit: 0.01 ¥Ø)"
,,,The percentage of the maximum current to the rated motor current is larger than 500%.,Check the setup value for each of Pr9.07 (Maximum instantaneous motor current) (Setting unit: 0.1 A) and Pr9.06 (Rated effective motor current) (Setting unit: 0.1 Arms).
60,3,Linear motor automatic setting error,RTEX communication has been established during automatic linear motor setup (during automatic scale direction/CS setting and during automatic current gain adjustment),Make sure that no RTEX communication will be established during automatic linear motor setting (during automatic scale direction/CS setting and during automatic current gain adjustment)
,,,"After automatic linear motor setting, RTEX communication has been established with the power supply not turned ON again.","After automatic linear motor setting, establish communication with the host device after the power supply is turned ON."
,,,A feedback current value has been overshot respective to the torque command during automatic linear motor setting.,"If there is current overshooting present, make adjustments such as by reducing the current gain."
61,0,Magnet pole position estimation error 1,Magnet pole position estimation has not been finished correctly.,Check the direction of the feedback scale
,,,"- Wrong feedback scale direction setting 
- Shortage of torque command/command time at the time of magnet pole position estimation",Adjust Pr9.22 (Torque command time for magnet pole position estimation) and Pr9.23 (Command torque for magnet pole position estimation).
,,,"- Use of the vertical axis 
- An unbalanced load and a large friction",The magnet pole position estimation function cannot be used for the vertical axis and an axis with an unbalanced load and a large friction.
61,1,Magnet pole position estimation error 2,The motor has not stopped after the elapse of the time set using Pr9.27 (Motor stop control time for magnet pole position estimation).,Increase the setup value for Pr9.27.
,,,,Check for unbalanced loads in the setup environment. (Does the motor operate even when with torque command = 0 ?)
61,2,Magnet pole position estimation error 3,A value of 3 has been set to Pr9.20 (Magnet pole detection scheme selection) with magnet pole position estimation never executed.,"Temporarily use Pr9.20 = 2 and perform magnet pole position estimation once. Then use Pr9.20 = 3, and this error will not be activated."
,,,A value of 3 has been set to Pr9.20 when a feedback scale that is not of the absolute type is in use.,Check that the feedback scale is of the absolute type.
70,0,(U-phase Current detector error),Control circuit has malfunctioned due to excess noise or other causes.,"Turn off the power once, then re-enter. If error repeats, this might be a failure."
,,,Some error has occurred inside of the driver while triggering self-diagnosis function of the driver.,"Stop using the products, and replace the motor and the driver. Return the products to the dealer or manufacturer."
